8,"conviction"],[3.175,0.362,"Verse"],[3.55,0.95,"seventy-eight"],[4.9,0.412,"Wherever"],[5.325,0.125,"there"],[5.463,0.15,"will"],[5.625,0.113,"be"],[5.75,0.25,"both"],[6.013,0.537,"Krishna"],[6.725,0.087,"the"],[6.825,0.25,"Lord"],[7.088,0.1,"of"],[7.2,0.487,"yoga"],[7.875,0.113,"or"],[8.0,0.463,"Dharma"],[8.475,0.087,"in"],[8.575,0.087,"the"],[8.675,0.263,"form"],[8.95,0.087,"of"],[9.05,0.087,"the"],[9.15,0.575,"scriptures"],[10.0,0.15,"and"],[10.162,0.487,"Arjuna"],[10.662,0.15,"with"],[10.825,0.075,"the"],[10.912,0.375,"weapons"],[11.3,0.125,"of"],[11.438,0.362,"duty"],[11.812,0.087,"and"],[11.912,0.637,"protection"],[12.875,0.087,"there"],[12.975,0.138,"will"],[13.125,0.163,"be"],[13.3,0.637,"everlasting"],[13.95,0.75,"prosperity"],[14.95,0.512,"victory"],[15.713,0.562,"happiness"],[16.45,0.1,"and"],[16.562,0.662,"morality"],[17.625,0.237,"This"],[17.875,0.138,"is"],[18.025,0.175,"my"],[18.212,0.812,"conviction"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"After the Gita","visual":["Arjuna picks up his bow","The war lasts eighteen days","Dharma prevails, at a great cost"],"L":[],"beyond":true,"say":"Our book ends here. What happens next comes from the Mahabharata. Arjuna picks up his bow. The war lasts eighteen days, and it is terrible. In the end, dharma prevails, and the Pandavas rule with justice, but they grieve for everyone they lost. The Gita never pretends that doing right is painless. It only promises that it is right.","start":285.96,"at":286.536,"end":310.656,"words":[[0.113,0.225,"Our"],[0.35,0.287,"book"],[0.65,0.287,"ends"],[0.95,0.375,"here"],[1.725,0.225,"What"],[1.962,0.537,"happens"],[2.513,0.362,"next"],[2.888,0.388,"comes"],[3.288,0.188,"from"],[3.487,0.087,"the"],[3.587,1.062,"Mahabharata"],[5.05,0.6,"Arjuna"],[5.662,0.3,"picks"],[5.975,0.15,"up"],[6.138,0.175,"his"],[6.325,0.4,"bow"],[7.125,0.087,"The"],[7.225,0.2,"war"],[7.438,0.5,"lasts"],[7.95,0.438,"eighteen"],[8.4,0.45,"days"],[9.1,0.113,"and"],[9.225,0.125,"it"],[9.363,0.125,"is"],[9.5,0.6,"terrible"],[10.5,0.125,"In"],[10.637,0.163,"the"],[10.812,0.35,"end"],[11.375,0.325,"dharma"],[11.713,0.65,"prevails"],[12.575,0.113,"and"],[12.7,0.1,"the"],[12.812,0.637,"Pandavas"],[13.463,0.275,"rule"],[13.75,0.175,"with"],[13.938,0.575,"justice"],[14.8,0.15,"but"],[14.963,0.138,"they"],[15.113,0.388,"grieve"],[15.512,0.125,"for"],[15.65,0.45,"everyone"],[16.113,0.1,"they"],[16.225,0.575,"lost"],[17.2,0.113,"The"],[17.325,0.438,"Gita"],[17.775,0.312,"never"],[18.1,0.6,"pretends"],[18.712,0.188,"that"],[18.913,0.3,"doing"],[19.225,0.3,"right"],[19.538,0.113,"is"],[19.663,0.688,"painless"],[20.75,0.15,"It"],[20.913,0.287,"only"],[21.212,0.65,"promises"],[21.875,0.188,"that"],[22.075,0.125,"it"],[22.212,0.138,"is"],[22.363,0.525,"right"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"True Renunciation Is Releasing Attachment to Results, Not Abandoning Duty","visual":["Keep doing service, charity and austerity","Give up attachment to their fruits","Abandoning duty is delusion"],"L":["L1"],"say":"Lesson one. True renunciation is releasing attachment to results, not abandoning duty. Service, charity and discipline purify the one who does them, so they must not be dropped. What is given up is the craving for their fruits. Walking away from duty out of delusion or fear is not renunciation.","start":310.656,"at":311.232,"end":332.76,"words":[[0.125,0.45,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.45,"one"],[1.413,0.263,"True"],[1.688,0.95,"renunciation"],[2.65,0.175,"is"],[2.837,0.475,"releasing"],[3.325,0.688,"attachment"],[4.025,0.087,"to"],[4.125,0.562,"results"],[4.938,0.212,"not"],[5.162,0.562,"abandoning"],[5.737,0.5,"duty"],[6.625,0.675,"Service"],[7.525,0.625,"charity"],[8.238,0.15,"and"],[8.4,0.55,"discipline"],[8.963,0.6,"purify"],[9.575,0.1,"the"],[9.688,0.212,"one"],[9.912,0.138,"who"],[10.062,0.25,"does"],[10.325,0.25,"them"],[10.875,0.113,"so"],[11.0,0.113,"they"],[11.125,0.275,"must"],[11.412,0.2,"not"],[11.625,0.113,"be"],[11.75,0.525,"dropped"],[12.65,0.237,"What"],[12.9,0.138,"is"],[13.05,0.3,"given"],[13.363,0.3,"up"],[13.675,0.163,"is"],[13.85,0.1,"the"],[13.963,0.487,"craving"],[14.463,0.125,"for"],[14.6,0.138,"their"],[14.75,0.65,"fruits"],[15.8,0.425,"Walking"],[16.238,0.312,"away"],[16.562,0.225,"from"],[16.8,0.487,"duty"],[17.3,0.212,"out"],[17.525,0.113,"of"],[17.65,0.65,"delusion"],[18.312,0.113,"or"],[18.438,0.45,"fear"],[18.9,0.163,"is"],[19.075,0.263,"not"],[19.35,0.938,"renunciation"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Five Causes Drive Every Action — Not the Self Alone","visual":["The body, the doer, the senses","The life forces, and providence","No one is the sole doer of anything"],"L":["L2"],"say":"Lesson two. Five causes drive every action, not the Self alone. The body, the doer, the senses, the life forces and providence all play their part. Whoever understands this stops claiming sole credit, or sole blame, and is not bound by what they do.","start":332.76,"at":333.336,"end":351.528,"words":[[0.113,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.463,"two"],[1.438,0.388,"Five"],[1.837,0.487,"causes"],[2.337,0.338,"drive"],[2.688,0.275,"every"],[2.975,0.487,"action"],[3.737,0.212,"not"],[3.962,0.1,"the"],[4.075,0.3,"Self"],[4.388,0.5,"alone"],[5.287,0.125,"The"],[5.425,0.438,"body"],[6.062,0.125,"the"],[6.2,0.362,"doer"],[6.787,0.1,"the"],[6.9,0.637,"senses"],[7.763,0.087,"the"],[7.862,0.287,"life"],[8.162,0.487,"forces"],[8.662,0.113,"and"],[8.787,0.625,"providence"],[9.425,0.225,"all"],[9.662,0.225,"play"],[9.9,0.138,"their"],[10.05,0.55,"part"],[11.0,0.425,"Whoever"],[11.438,0.713,"understands"],[12.162,0.188,"this"],[12.363,0.362,"stops"],[12.738,0.412,"claiming"],[13.162,0.287,"sole"],[13.463,0.463,"credit"],[14.15,0.1,"or"],[14.262,0.3,"sole"],[14.575,0.375,"blame"],[15.238,0.087,"and"],[15.338,0.113,"is"],[15.463,0.237,"not"],[15.713,0.362,"bound"],[16.087,0.138,"by"],[16.238,0.2,"what"],[16.45,0.138,"they"],[16.6,0.362,"do"]]},{"layout":"compare","headline":"Goodness and passion in action","visual":["Goodness | Passion","Sees one Reality in all | Sees only separate things","Acts from duty, without ego | Acts from ego and craving","Steady in success and failure | Tossed by joy and sorrow"],"L":["L3"],"say":"Lesson three. Knowledge, action and the doer all come in three modes. In goodness, one sees one Reality in all beings, acts from duty without ego, and stays steady in success and failure. In passion, one sees only separate things and acts from ego and craving. In ignorance, one clings to a single thing as if it were everything, and acts carelessly.","start":351.528,"at":352.104,"end":376.584,"words":[[0.113,0.475,"Lesson"],[0.6,0.512,"three"],[1.5,0.562,"Knowledge"],[2.288,0.525,"action"],[2.913,0.113,"and"],[3.038,0.113,"the"],[3.163,0.287,"doer"],[3.462,0.263,"all"],[3.737,0.225,"come"],[3.975,0.125,"in"],[4.112,0.25,"three"],[4.375,0.55,"modes"],[5.325,0.138,"In"],[5.475,0.562,"goodness"],[6.25,0.263,"one"],[6.525,0.3,"sees"],[6.838,0.212,"one"],[7.062,0.575,"Reality"],[7.65,0.138,"in"],[7.8,0.175,"all"],[7.987,0.5,"beings"],[8.762,0.275,"acts"],[9.05,0.175,"from"],[9.238,0.362,"duty"],[9.613,0.4,"without"],[10.025,0.375,"ego"],[10.65,0.138,"and"],[10.8,0.325,"stays"],[11.137,0.35,"steady"],[11.5,0.113,"in"],[11.625,0.475,"success"],[12.113,0.1,"and"],[12.225,0.537,"failure"],[13.162,0.15,"In"],[13.325,0.537,"passion"],[14.15,0.225,"one"],[14.387,0.312,"sees"],[14.713,0.263,"only"],[14.988,0.425,"separate"],[15.425,0.425,"things"],[15.863,0.163,"and"],[16.038,0.338,"acts"],[16.387,0.188,"from"],[16.587,0.412,"ego"],[17.012,0.138,"and"],[17.163,0.575,"craving"],[18.137,0.138,"In"],[18.288,0.613,"ignorance"],[19.15,0.263,"one"],[19.425,0.388,"clings"],[19.825,0.125,"to"],[19.962,0.062,"a"],[20.038,0.388,"single"],[20.438,0.375,"thing"],[20.825,0.113,"as"],[20.95,0.113,"if"],[21.075,0.087,"it"],[21.175,0.138,"were"],[21.325,0.588,"everything"],[22.125,0.125,"and"],[22.262,0.287,"acts"],[22.562,0.688,"carelessly"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Intellect and Resolve Also Come in Three Modes","visual":["Goodness: knows right from wrong","Passion: confuses them","Ignorance: calls wrong right"],"L":["L4"],"say":"Lesson four. Intellect and resolve also come in three modes. An intellect in goodness clearly knows right from wrong, bondage from freedom. In passion, it confuses them. In ignorance, it calls wrong right. And resolve, too, can serve God, serve desire, or serve only sleep, fear and despair.","start":376.584,"at":377.16,"end":399.336,"words":[[0.138,0.438,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.463,"four"],[1.425,0.637,"Intellect"],[2.075,0.113,"and"],[2.2,0.588,"resolve"],[2.8,0.388,"also"],[3.2,0.237,"come"],[3.45,0.125,"in"],[3.587,0.275,"three"],[3.875,0.562,"modes"],[4.812,0.138,"An"],[4.963,0.537,"intellect"],[5.513,0.125,"in"],[5.65,0.525,"goodness"],[6.188,0.375,"clearly"],[6.575,0.287,"knows"],[6.875,0.275,"right"],[7.162,0.225,"from"],[7.4,0.362,"wrong"],[8.025,0.425,"bondage"],[8.463,0.188,"from"],[8.662,0.525,"freedom"],[9.562,0.175,"In"],[9.75,0.562,"passion"],[10.537,0.113,"it"],[10.662,0.637,"confuses"],[11.312,0.312,"them"],[12.025,0.125,"In"],[12.162,0.637,"ignorance"],[13.037,0.1,"it"],[13.15,0.362,"calls"],[13.525,0.275,"wrong"],[13.812,0.487,"right"],[14.675,0.15,"And"],[14.838,0.6,"resolve"],[15.65,0.375,"too"],[16.225,0.188,"can"],[16.425,0.312,"serve"],[16.75,0.338,"God"],[17.35,0.3,"serve"],[17.663,0.588,"desire"],[18.5,0.138,"or"],[18.65,0.325,"serve"],[18.988,0.25,"only"],[19.25,0.475,"sleep"],[19.925,0.35,"fear"],[20.288,0.1,"and"],[20.4,0.55,"despair"]]},{"layout":"compare","headline":"Two kinds of pleasure","visual":["Spiritual practice | Sense pleasure","Poison at first | Nectar at first","Nectar in the end | Poison in the end","Ends sorrow | Ends in sorrow"],"L":["L5"],"say":"Lesson five. The highest pleasure is bitter at first and sweet at the end. The joy of spiritual practice can feel like poison at the start, and becomes nectar. Sense pleasure is nectar at the start, and turns to poison. And the pleasure of laziness and delusion confuses us from beginning to end.","start":399.336,"at":399.912,"end":420.192,"words":[[0.1,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.575,0.575,"five"],[1.55,0.075,"The"],[1.637,0.438,"highest"],[2.087,0.463,"pleasure"],[2.562,0.175,"is"],[2.75,0.3,"bitter"],[3.062,0.175,"at"],[3.25,0.512,"first"],[3.775,0.138,"and"],[3.925,0.35,"sweet"],[4.287,0.075,"at"],[4.375,0.138,"the"],[4.525,0.4,"end"],[5.325,0.138,"The"],[5.475,0.275,"joy"],[5.763,0.15,"of"],[5.925,0.562,"spiritual"],[6.5,0.575,"practice"],[7.088,0.2,"can"],[7.3,0.25,"feel"],[7.562,0.225,"like"],[7.8,0.438,"poison"],[8.25,0.1,"at"],[8.363,0.087,"the"],[8.463,0.475,"start"],[9.213,0.087,"and"],[9.312,0.412,"becomes"],[9.738,0.5,"nectar"],[10.625,0.375,"Sense"],[11.012,0.463,"pleasure"],[11.488,0.175,"is"],[11.675,0.35,"nectar"],[12.037,0.113,"at"],[12.162,0.1,"the"],[12.275,0.512,"start"],[13.05,0.1,"and"],[13.162,0.375,"turns"],[13.55,0.087,"to"],[13.65,0.575,"poison"],[14.625,0.125,"And"],[14.762,0.113,"the"],[14.887,0.475,"pleasure"],[15.375,0.113,"of"],[15.5,0.613,"laziness"],[16.125,0.113,"and"],[16.25,0.688,"delusion"],[16.95,0.637,"confuses"],[17.6,0.2,"us"],[17.812,0.175,"from"],[18.0,0.4,"beginning"],[18.413,0.15,"to"],[18.575,0.463,"end"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Division of Labor Is Based on Natural Ability, Not Birth","visual":["Four kinds of work, by natural qualities","Not by the family one is born into","Your own work, done well, is worship"],"L":["L6"],"say":"Lesson six. The division of labour is based on natural ability, not birth. Thinkers, protectors, merchants and workers are defined by their inner qualities and gifts, not by their family. And doing one's own natural work, offered to God, is a path to perfection.","start":420.192,"at":420.768,"end":439.752,"words":[[0.125,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.6,0.588,"six"],[1.587,0.113,"The"],[1.712,0.412,"division"],[2.138,0.1,"of"],[2.25,0.5,"labour"],[2.763,0.188,"is"],[2.962,0.362,"based"],[3.337,0.138,"on"],[3.487,0.388,"natural"],[3.888,0.55,"ability"],[4.725,0.263,"not"],[5.0,0.512,"birth"]